    ],
    "rationale": "At matched u and h, dev responses differ strongly between constant positive and negative histories. The size of that contrast is smaller at h=1.2 than at h=0.3, consistent with waiting-time attenuation of prior-drive influence. Impulse and alternating-history observations also distinguish older from more recent intervals. This joint model represents those contrasts with an age-weighted history summary and waiting-time decay while retaining a simple current-drive baseline. The supplied evidence motivates this form but does not establish a unique mechanism or guarantee the dev threshold; all parameters must be refit on fit data and evaluated on dev.",
    "scientific_change": "Replace the current-state-only response with a joint model in which current drive contributes linearly and prior drive contributes through an age-weighted summary attenuated by waiting time."
